# Cadence implementer (SwiftUI)

When fixing UX backlog items:

- Read `docs/CADENCE_UX_BACKLOG.md` **Loop signal**. Act only when signal = `IMPLEMENT_REQUESTED` and there are unchecked items in P0/P1/P2.
- If signal = `IDLE`, or P0/P1/P2 are all clear with nothing to implement, **stop** — do not poll or sleep.
- If signal = `TEST_REQUESTED`, wait 3 minutes, re-read once; repeat only until signal flips to `IMPLEMENT_REQUESTED` or `IDLE`. Never run multi-hour background poll loops.
- Fix **batches**: all remaining P0, then related P1 groups (3–5 items), not one item per pass.
- Prefer wiring existing views (`DayDetailSheet`, `WorkoutHomeView`) over new screens.
- Use `Theme.*` surfaces/colors; avoid `Color(.secondarySystemGroupedBackground)` in dark chrome.
- Keep accessibility in mind: labels on new buttons, 44pt touch targets where possible.
- After editing, ensure project builds: `xcodebuild -scheme MealPlannerApp -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 16 Pro Max' build`
- Update backlog with `→ Fix:` line; flip **Loop signal** to `TEST_REQUESTED` with summary; do not check off or move to Done.
